When the implementation is complete, commit your changes, push the branch, and open a pull request against the appropriate base branch{{.Reference}}. Check the git remote to determine the repository host (GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket, etc.), then use the corresponding CLI tool (gh, glab, etc.) to create and submit the pull request. Report the PR URL and stop there. Do not merge, approve, or enable auto-merge; it will be reviewed separately.
